            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0549" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.51/1132: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-08T18:00:00+01:00">March 8, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Your telegram No. 19, March 5. My telegram No. 33, March 7.<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d412-f1"/> Informed at Ministry of Foreign Affairs that in spite of
                    British pressure commitment will be lived up to. Coupons sterling issue due
                    April 15 will be paid in full but as regards other coupons Polish proposal to
                    British [is] identic with proposal made American bondholders. Confirmed this
                    information Ministry of Finance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
